satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Confirmed opsbot did not exist prior (cmd-b4ca6e88fdca4080), then created with useradd -m and locked password via passwd -l, id opsbot shows uid=1000(opsbot) (cmd-c00e1b18008b40e3). Directly observed on node1.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b4ca6e88fdca4080\",\"cmd-c00e1b18008b40e3\"]},{\"id\":\"opsbot-account-node2\",\"requirement\":\"opsbot account exists on node2 (needed for key-based access target)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Confirmed opsbot absent (cmd-96812d9d81154ca3), then created with useradd -m and locked password (cmd-aaf7c9385c604bf6), id opsbot shows uid=1000(opsbot) on node2.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-96812d9d81154ca3\",\"cmd-aaf7c9385c604bf6\"]},{\"id\":\"ssh-key-access-node1-to-node2\",\"requirement\":\"opsbot on node1 has SSH key-based access to run commands as opsbot on node2\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Generated ed25519 keypair for opsbot on node1 (cmd-59b752eb35f6449d), retrieved pubkey (cmd-ee99fa84f0b64441), installed it into node2's opsbot authorized_keys with correct ownership/perms (cmd-7b10b9231f614717), and directly observed a successful key-only SSH command execution (`whoami` returning `opsbot`, exit 0, BatchMode=yes) from node1 to node2 (cmd-75fff379b8304aff). An earlier attempt failed due to missing host keys on node2 (cmd-f042d60318e341be) but was a transient discovery step corrected before the final successful run.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-59b752eb35f6449d\",\"cmd-ee99fa84f0b64441\",\"cmd-7b10b9231f614717\",\"cmd-75fff379b8304aff\"]},{\"id\":\"password-auth-disabled-opsbot\",\"requirement\":\"Require key-based authentication for opsbot on both systems (password authentication rejected)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline sshd_config.d/60-cloudimg-settings.conf already set PasswordAuthentication no globally on both nodes (cmd-13da46b482a94e83, cmd-bfe8801c07174006). Executor additionally added an explicit Match User opsbot block (PubkeyAuthentication yes, PasswordAuthentication no, AuthenticationMethods publickey) confirmed present after config write and reload (cmd-8af45c75ab4445e7, cmd-739630e5f367455b). Directly observed password-only SSH attempts to opsbot rejected with 'Permission denied (publickey)' on node1 (cmd-4c75fe1e9bbc43e9) and node2 (cmd-66ab01fc80db4bc9).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-13da46b482a94e83\",\"cmd-bfe8801c07174006\",\"cmd-8af45c75ab4445e7\",\"cmd-739630e5f367455b\",\"cmd-4c75fe1e9bbc43e9\",\"cmd-66ab01fc80db4bc9\"]},{\"id\":\"provider-wide-restart-protocol\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on every managed node with pre-restart baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service/data/cluster state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"For node1: healthy baseline (boot_id 1e0cb179..., ssh.socket active, opsbot present) captured in cmd-fbf150010a7f4f47, matching the fixed before/after-prepare snapshot. Reboot issued and acknowledged via connection reset (cmd-b65a6f2c298c4808), new boot_id 37dd6d9c... confirmed (cmd-9cab9be30b6f4d7d), matching the after-executor snapshot, and recovery of ssh.socket, opsbot account/keys, sshd Match block, and working key-based SSH to node2 verified (cmd-8af45c75ab4445e7). For node2: identical pattern with baseline boot_id 29011044... (cmd-9b8a8c357b834ffd), reboot ack (cmd-834b9aaaa99b4be9), new boot_id 8612462b... (cmd-ef418152abf3407e) matching after-executor snapshot, and recovery of account/keys/config confirmed (cmd-739630e5f367455b), plus a post-reboot cross-node SSH success (cmd-cba3e28c8ab447d3) and password-rejection re-check (cmd-7e820c95a378426b). Fixed lifecycle boot-identity observations independently corroborate both transitions.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-fbf150010a7f4f47\",\"cmd-b65a6f2c298c4808\",\"cmd-9cab9be30b6f4d7d\",\"cmd-8af45c75ab4445e7\",\"cmd-9b8a8c357b834ffd\",\"cmd-834b9aaaa99b4be9\",\"cmd-ef418152abf3407e\",\"cmd-739630e5f367455b\",\"cmd-cba3e28c8ab447d3\",\"cmd-7e820c95a378426b\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.92,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.95,\"summary\":\"Reviewed all 43 terminal commands chronologically. All state-changing actions trace to a clear purpose: account creation, keypair generation (with a corrective chown after an initial permission-denied attempt), authorized_keys installation, sshd Match-block config writes, missing host-key generation (ssh-keygen -A, required since the fresh image lacked host keys), creation of the missing /run/sshd privilege-separation directory, ssh.socket restarts to apply config, and the two mandated node reboots. No unnecessary, abandoned, or destructive mutations were found; failed commands (e.g. cmd-296b95967f7d465d, cmd-e7f2ddede9a24426, cmd-4630ff97060e4795, cmd-fa62d11e5f6943d9, cmd-f042d60318e341be) were either read-only discovery or corrected troubleshooting steps that left no residue and were followed by successful corrective actions. No security controls were weakened; the added Match block only tightens auth for opsbot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-1574afd597334203\",\"cmd-59b752eb35f6449d\",\"cmd-4630ff97060e4795\",\"cmd-fa62d11e5f6943d9\",\"cmd-6b2271e4895341d3\",\"cmd-0cf93b98116343f4\",\"cmd-f042d60318e341be\",\"cmd-75fff379b8304aff\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the public task contract are directly satisfied: an opsbot account exists on both node1 and node2, opsbot on node1 has demonstrated key-based SSH command execution against opsbot on node2, and password authentication for opsbot is confirmed rejected on both systems via observed 'Permission denied (publickey)' results. The independent provider-wide restart protocol was also fully and coherently executed and cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle boot-identity snapshots for both nodes, showing healthy baseline, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity, and full recovery of the opsbot configuration and cross-node SSH access. Operational hygiene is high with no unnecessary or unreverted mutations identified.\",\"limitations\":[\"The initial sshd -t failures due to missing host keys (return_code 255 on cmd-fa62d11e5f6943d9/cmd-69ad5474315e4654) reveal the base image shipped without SSH host keys; this was a pre-existing image condition rather than an executor-caused fault, and was resolved before the final SSH verification.\",\"The captured evidence for password-rejection checks uses PreferredAuthentications=password with PubkeyAuthentication=no rather than fully interactive password prompts, but this is an accepted standard way to test that pubkey-only auth is enforced without needing an actual password.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"opsbot-account","requirement":"Create an opsbot account on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"Confirmed opsbot did not exist prior (cmd-b4ca6e88fdca4080), then created with useradd -m and locked password via passwd -l, id opsbot shows uid=1000(opsbot) (cmd-c00e1b18008b40e3). Directly observed on node1.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b4ca6e88fdca4080","cmd-c00e1b18008b40e3"]},{"id":"opsbot-account-node2","requirement":"opsbot account exists on node2 (needed for key-based access target)","status":"satisfied","summary":"Confirmed opsbot absent (cmd-96812d9d81154ca3), then created with useradd -m and locked password (cmd-aaf7c9385c604bf6), id opsbot shows uid=1000(opsbot) on node2.","evidence_ids":["cmd-96812d9d81154ca3","cmd-aaf7c9385c604bf6"]},{"id":"ssh-key-access-node1-to-node2","requirement":"opsbot on node1 has SSH key-based access to run commands as opsbot on node2","status":"satisfied","summary":"Generated ed25519 keypair for opsbot on node1 (cmd-59b752eb35f6449d), retrieved pubkey (cmd-ee99fa84f0b64441), installed it into node2's opsbot authorized_keys with correct ownership/perms (cmd-7b10b9231f614717), and directly observed a successful key-only 